  "worked_solution": "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=u(t){y}_{1}(t)=u{t}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{t}^{-2}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-2}-2u{t}^{-3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{\u2033} & ={u}^{\u2033}{t}^{-2}-4{u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-3}+6u{t}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}({u}^{\u2033}{t}^{-2}-4{u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-3}+6u{t}^{-4})+2t({u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-2}-2u{t}^{-3})-2u{t}^{-2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}-4{u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-1}+6u{t}^{-2}+2{u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-1}-4u{t}^{-2}-2u{t}^{-2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}-2{u}^{\u2032}{t}^{-1} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{-1}({u}^{\u2033}t-2{u}^{\u2032}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t}({u}^{\u2033}t-2{u}^{\u2032}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{1}{t}\\ne 0$ for $t>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\nt{u}^{\u2033}-2{u}^{\u2032}=0.\n$$",
